{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/75984-angels","id":75984,"title":"Angels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-20T17:36:18-08:00","id":75984,"title":"Angels","content":"So guys do you have to lose cover and then the GM brings these guys in or can he just choose to when ever he wishes in terms of plot. E.g like clash of worlds Vampires gets attack by angles or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2338-nagumyrehal","name":"nagumyrehal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2338_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T17:52:40-08:00","id":75995,"title":"","content":"The God Machine can send in angels when it thinks it needs them, but most of the time using them like shock-troops is wasteful, it's quite likely to try to use mortals first, or perhaps even trick other vampires into doing it.<br /> The God Machine, however, isn't aware of where Demons are, due to their cover, until they break it somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T19:57:20-08:00","id":76058,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine can't just pop out an Angel whenever it wants. It needs to manipulate some occult physics via Infrastructure in order to bring a new Angel into existence or give new orders to an existing one. Neither one of these is something to be done lightly; I doubt there are many Angels that just sort of randomly patrol. There are a few Conditions that would justify dispatching an Angel, and frequently using a bunch of powerful Embeds/Exploits might garner some fair attention, but chances are, there isn't an Angel around every corner, waiting for your Cover to drop a single dot.<br /> <br /> In short; largely Storyteller fiat, but should only occur when rightly provoked by the actions of the ring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T20:14:37-08:00","id":76065,"title":"","content":"Losing cover allows the God-Machine to know a Demon is around. How it responds is up to the ST but normally, unless the Demon is messing with Infrastructure, getting in the way of one of the projects, or the God-Machine simply needs the Demon for something, it won't be overtly hostile vs sending someone to keep tabs on said Demon so it doesn't get in the way of plans or easy access should the God-Machine decide to spend the effort to capture and reprocess it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T07:21:05-08:00","id":76262,"title":"","content":"How I did it in my Demon game was that there were a few angels already in Las Vegas with particular missions. The PC's only ran afoul of them when they started doing things; it was more that humans and a particular stigmatic were the antagonists. The angels were just backdrop - and one of them is actually an Exile of sorts. She's turned into a very special case, and I very much like her story. As all of my WoD games are intertwined, she's popped up in other games since and it's been rather interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T14:30:36-08:00","id":77827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/75984-angels?p=75995#post75995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God Machine can send in angels when it thinks it needs them, but most of the time using them like shock-troops is wasteful, it's quite likely to try to use mortals first, or perhaps even trick other vampires into doing it.<br /> The God Machine, however, isn't aware of where Demons are, due to their cover, until they break it somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kk so if There something the god machine wants to protect angles could be deployed as to say stay away from my S***.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/75984-angels?p=76262#post76262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I did it in my Demon game was that there were a few angels already in Las Vegas with particular missions. The PC's only ran afoul of them when they started doing things; it was more that humans and a particular stigmatic were the antagonists. The angels were just backdrop - and one of them is actually an Exile of sorts. She's turned into a very special case, and I very much like her story. As all of my WoD games are intertwined, she's popped up in other games since and it's been rather interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah angles npcs sound like an awesome idea, players talk to this guy one player says i punch him.........................run!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! oh God run! run! :'D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2338-nagumyrehal","name":"nagumyrehal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2338_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T18:08:27-08:00","id":77945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nagumyrehal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/75984-angels?p=77827#post77827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah angles npcs sound like an awesome idea, players talk to this guy one player says i punch him.........................run!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! oh God run! run! :'D</div> </div> </div> </div>Well actually, the particular NPC hasn't gotten into a fight with any PC in either of the two games she's been in (Los Angeles mortals/Las Vegas Demon). In fact, no PC has ever even seen her in combat, nor do they have any idea what her capabilities are. In fact, they aren't even 100% sure she's an angel...they just know there is <i>something</i> &quot;wrong&quot; with her, and they strongly suspect she's an angel. She's simply been a joy to play, and it's so much fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T04:03:47-08:00","id":78218,"title":"","content":"I like my angels as NPC figures to interact with. And each one have something about them that could lead them to fall. Hate demons? Even to the point of running away from your mission to chase one? Uh, oh, broken and disconnected. Another angel NPC was a hunter-angel tempter who worked to convince demons to come back to the God Machine. Both were stolen directly from the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}